{"arrivo":"fa","origine":"trk-pro","origine_nome":"Proto-Turkic","n":6,"parole":[{"parola":"اردو","pos":"noun|adj","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"horde","termine_origine":"*ordu","catena":[{"codice":"trk-pro","nome":"Proto-Turkic","termine":"*ordu","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"trk-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Derived from Proto-Turkic *ordu (“army, camp”) (see Azerbaijani ordu, Turkish ordu, Turkmen orda). Compare horde."},{"parola":"بیگ","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"perhaps","significato":"bey; a former aristocratic title in Iran, Central Asia, South Asia and Turkey.","termine_origine":"*bēg","catena":[{"codice":"trk-pro","nome":"Proto-Turkic","termine":"*bēg","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"trk","nome":"Turkic","termine":"Turkic","categoria":"prestito"},{"codice":"ira-mid","nome":"Middle Iranian","termine":"","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"ira-mid","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Borrowed from Proto-Turkic *bēg via a Turkic language, perhaps ultimately from Middle Iranian, in which case it is a doublet of فغ (faġ, “idol; companion, friend”)."},{"parola":"بیگم","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"perhaps","significato":"begum","termine_origine":"*bēg","catena":[{"codice":"trk-pro","nome":"Proto-Turkic","termine":"*bēg","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"trk-pro","ambiti":["sport"],"via":"","testo":"From بیگ (beyg, “titled man, chief”) (from Proto-Turkic *bēg; see there for more) and the genitive enclitic -em, or perhaps from بگم (bagam, “queen”). Cognate with Azerbaijani bəyim, Ottoman Turkish بكم (beyim), Uzbek begim. Compare خانم (xânom)."},{"parola":"طوی","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"wedding","termine_origine":"*toy","catena":[{"codice":"trk-pro","nome":"Proto-Turkic","termine":"*toy","categoria":"non_preci